-- S0-4 (review round of `ffi-lower-and-link`): the `mdk_` prefix is the Medaka
-- runtime's own C symbol namespace (`runtime/medaka_rt.c`), and a foreign
-- declaration's name is used VERBATIM as the C symbol it links to.  With no
-- reserved-prefix check, this declaration linked onto the runtime's real
-- internal `mdk_nil` and printed its Nil constructor word (562949953421315) at
-- exit 0.
--
-- 🚨 THE SIGNATURE HERE MATCHES the internal ON PURPOSE, because that is the
-- SILENT half.  A mismatched one was already loud (clang rejects the conflicting
-- `declare`), so a cell built on a mismatch would have passed against the broken
-- compiler too.
--
-- ⚠️ Not the same rule as `ffi_builtin_shadow_reject.mdk`.  That one is about
-- INCOMPATIBILITY with a legitimate catalog builtin and admits the compatible
-- case; this one is an unconditional namespace ban, with no signature test and
-- no catalog-name exemption -- the catalog holds no `mdk_`-prefixed row, so the
-- two rules cannot collide.
extern mdk_nil : Unit -> <FFI> Int

main : <IO, FFI> Unit
main = println (mdk_nil ())
